<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ptolemy I Soter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">founded kingdom 305 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Ptolemy I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ptolemy I Soter was a Macedonian general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> who became ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> after Alexander's death. He took the royal title in 305 BCE, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic Empire</a>. During the wars of the successors he was at times an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucus-i-nicator">Seleucus I</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ptolemy-i-soter.jpg" alt="Ptolemy I Soter" width="280" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marie-Lan Nguyen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ptolemy_I_Soter_Louvre_Ma849_A.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
